<div class="widget editor pageStyles narrow" id="divEditor0fdd4508-7653-4d1f-b8ec-2c835222f7ec" data-elementqueryclasses='{"wide-narrow":"min-width:25em"}'>
	    <div class="fr-view">


        <p><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;">Posted September 8, 2026</span></p><p><span style="font-size: 20px;"><strong>Countywide Charter Amendment - County Commission Single Member Districts</strong></span><br><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong><span style="color: rgb(192, 0, 0);">Florida Legislature Proposed Lee County Charter Amendment</span></strong></span></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px;">The Lee County Supervisor of Elections gives notice that on Tuesday, November 3, 2026, a special election will be conducted at which the voters of Lee County will be asked whether they approve or disapprove of the adoption of an amendment to the Lee County Charter regarding a County Charter Revision Relating to a Referendum Providing for the Structure of the County Legislative Branch for single-member districts.</span></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px;"><a href="/DocumentCenter/View/1083" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">Ballot Language (English / Spanish PDF)</a></span><br><span style="font-size: 18px;"><a href="/DocumentCenter/View/1084" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">Laws of Florida 2025-222 (English PDF)</a></span><br><span style="font-size: 18px;"><a href="/DocumentCenter/View/1085" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">Laws of Florida 2025-222 (Spanish PDF)</a></span></p><p><br></p><p data-pasted="true"><span style="font-size: 20px;"><strong>Countywide Charter Amendment - Constitutional Officer Term Limits</strong></span><br><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong><span style="color: rgb(192, 0, 0);">Lee County Board of County Commissioners Proposed Charter Amendment</span></strong></span></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px;">The Lee County Supervisor of Elections gives notice that on Tuesday, November 3, 2026, a special election will be conducted at which the voters of Lee County will be asked whether they approve or disapprove of the adoption of an amendment to the Lee County Charter regarding a County Charter Revision Relating to Setting the Number of Consecutive Terms of Elected Constitutional Officers.</span></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px;"><a href="/DocumentCenter/View/1080" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">Ballot Language (English / Spanish PDF)</a><br><a href="/DocumentCenter/View/1078" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">Public Notice (English PDF)</a><br></span><span style="font-size: 18px;"><a href="/DocumentCenter/View/1099" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">Public Notice (Spanish PDF)</a></span></p><p><span style="font-size: 18px;"><a href="/DocumentCenter/View/1081" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">Resolution 26-05-23 (English PDF)</a><br><a href="/DocumentCenter/View/1082" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">Resolution 26-05-23 (Spanish PDF)</a></span></p>
    </div>

